# Fixing Workflow

When fixing lint errors, test failures, or build issues, follow this process. Never skip steps.

## Step 1: Discover ALL Failures

Run the appropriate command before touching any code:

| Category | Discovery command |
|----------|-------------------|
| Lint / format | `make check` |
| Unit tests | `make test` |
| Coverage | `make test-cov` |
| Build (wheel/sdist) | `python -m build` |

Read the complete output.

## Step 2: Create a Task List of ALL Failures

Catalog every failure into a task list:
- One item per distinct error/failure
- Include file path and short description
- Mark all items as pending

Example:
```
[ ] pdf_markdown/output.py -- line too long (E501)
[ ] tests/test_cli.py -- "test_convert_uses_fallback" assertion fails
```

## Step 3: Fix Each Issue Individually

For each item:
1. Read the failing file and understand the root cause
2. Apply the minimal, correct fix
3. Verify the fix:
   - Lint: `ruff check <file>` or `ruff format <file>`
   - Test: `pytest tests/<test_file>.py -v`
4. Mark done only after verification passes

## Step 4: Do NOT Run Full Suite Until All Items Resolved

Iterate one at a time. Avoid long full runs while issues remain.

## Step 5: Run Full Suite to Confirm

Once all items are resolved:
1. Run `make check && make test`
2. If regressions appear, add them to the task list and fix
3. Repeat until clean
